1. Open Mozilla Firefox browser.
2. Launch Selenium IDE and open the existing project **Login Test**.
3. Select the required test case (TC1).
4. Right-click in the command list and select **Insert New Command**.
5. Insert the **Store Title** command.
6. Enter `title` as the value for storing the page title.
7. Insert the **Assert Title** command and set the Selenium IDE page title as the target.
8. Insert an **If** command in the test case.
9. Enter the condition `${title}=="Selenium"` to check the stored title.
10. Insert an **Open** command and set the target to the Selenium IDE page.
11. Insert the **End** command to close the conditional block.
12. Run test case **TC1** using the **Run Current Test** option.
13. Check the execution log for errors. Initially, the test may fail if the variable `${title}` is not defined correctly.
14. Correct the test commands and run TC1 again.
15. Verify that all commands are marked successful and the execution log displays successful completion.
16. Observe the browser output. The screenshot shows a **404 Element not found** page.
